{"id": "EUVD-2026-103683", "enisaUuid": "f38e5f6f-714e-3060-9dfe-47a1d724b7f4", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nxfs: fix cursor and pointer handling when recovering iunlink buckets\n\nLOLLM pointed out a bug in xlog_recover_iunlink_bucket:\n\n1. We don't null out prev_ip after releasing it, which can lead to UAF\n   problems if the inodegc flush call in the loop fails.\n\nat which point I noticed even more bugs:\n\n2. If the inodegc flush inside the loop fails, we also leak @ip.\n\n3. We set prev_agino to agino having already advanced agino, which\n   results in inodes with i_prev_unlinked set to itself.\n\n4. If we exit the bottom of the loop with prev_ip set, then prev_ip\n   aliases ip and we also set its i_prev_unlinked to itself.\n\nBugs 3 and 4 introduce loops into the unlinked list, though these loops\ndon't surface because we immediately flush each unlinked inode after\nloading it.\n\nFix all of these issues.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:14:53", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:55:04", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/47a948ba653a463d429e02fda2f06a3d6b78666d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8c9d5b8a96d6b93eb24e07b4163c89341ba29bd1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/66a2179d02668f8df44b1a249899006f3ba38ea0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/961c717e6bf0e53c2c2b1fe4aef1add9390fedab", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/65f39d09d73718611cee40399179323b5d4ead00"], "aliases": ["GHSA-27hr-pwp4-53ph", "CVE-2026-98443"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "353a6162-a0ba-33b4-b919-acb60f1d0f7c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "35c2eae3-f7ce-3cbc-9b6c-dc97cd26865c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "04755d2e5821b3afbaadd09fe5df58d04de36484 <65f39d09d73718611cee40399179323b5d4ead00"}, {"id": "508c72a3-4410-30b3-8711-73f6cfa6ace7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.0"}, {"id": "59d6a74f-4033-389b-b252-7f7688f2f9ce", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.9"}, {"id": "5bedaf8a-c0d2-34c1-8c3c-18db1a320c98", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "04755d2e5821b3afbaadd09fe5df58d04de36484 <961c717e6bf0e53c2c2b1fe4aef1add9390fedab"}, {"id": "5e543cca-7f20-3cb1-ae12-88743f113acb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "6bac715e-4a12-35b8-ad2c-021957551396", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.55"}, {"id": "8932519e-0a6f-32ea-9d7e-a0a2d3017922", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "aa0dea76-e150-3a29-bbe0-561e6d4c4fce", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "ac348d4d-f79f-3e27-ac3b-542aff866a76", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "04755d2e5821b3afbaadd09fe5df58d04de36484 <66a2179d02668f8df44b1a249899006f3ba38ea0"}, {"id": "cb92ee96-54a5-3eca-a30b-6603eb409480", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "04755d2e5821b3afbaadd09fe5df58d04de36484 <47a948ba653a463d429e02fda2f06a3d6b78666d"}, {"id": "e4c47d17-c137-3c09-8907-03bddaee46fa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "04755d2e5821b3afbaadd09fe5df58d04de36484 <8c9d5b8a96d6b93eb24e07b4163c89341ba29bd1"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "b6ee269d-f986-3e48-a9b4-9919e1b2552c", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}